# Files currently over the size limit, frozen at their present length.
#
# Scope is verify_code_size.py's, not "shell": linux/scripts, linux/host-config,
# docs/scripts and linux/llm-stack by *.sh/*.py, plus the Dockerfile* at the top of
# linux/. Seven of the rows below are llm-stack, in scope since EX1 (2026-09-07).
#
# Format: <path> | <lines> | <reason>
#
# Same four-way contract as function-size.allow: growth, a new offender, an
# unrecorded shrink and a stale entry all fail. Shrinking a file means updating
# its number here; deleting the line once it drops under the limit.
#
# The refactor entries live in docs/refactoring-backlog.md F2.
docs/scripts/bump_versions.py | 1090 | 1083 -> 1090 on 2026-10-07: protoc_from_protobuf_cmake, the slaved PROTOC_VERSION derivation that reads LiteRT-LM 0.18's LITERTLM_PROTOBUF_TAG cache variable (+7). 1078 -> 1083 on 2026-10-06: spec_wix_firewall and its table row, the WiX firewall extension the final stage installs (+5). 1065 -> 1078 on 2026-10-05: CON59 -- pin_files() and the per-file loops read and write tool-pins.env beside versions.env (+13). 1042 -> 1065 on 2026-10-01: CON50 -- spec_uv also refreshes UV_WINDOWS_ARM64_SHA256, the uv zip of the windows-11-arm pytest job (+1), and spec_chrome_for_testing (Google's bucket publishes md5 only, so it hashes the four zips) and the emulator's MANUAL rows and allowlisted SHA pair. PRIOR: 1236 -> 1042 on 2026-09-30: comment sweep. PRIOR: 1241 -> 1236 on 2026-09-29: -5 lines, the MANUAL rows for AMD's Windows torch, torchvision, device and bootstrap wheels went with their pins (the rocm lane builds torch from source) and the two source commits took one row. PRIOR: 1247 -> 1241 on 2026-09-29: -6 lines, spec_app_ref removed (never registered in SPECS, and APP_REF now tracks a branch, so a newest-tag bump is wrong). PRIOR: 1209 -> 1247 on 2026-09-23: +38 lines for the ORT WebGPU EP Dawn/DXC pins, the Vulkan runtime zip, llama.cpp Vulkan and the gfx1200/ai-edge-litert rows (spec functions and MANUAL rows the tier table names). PRIOR: 1116 -> 1209 on 2026-09-23: +93 lines for the rocm-lane pins (spec_amf_headers, spec_llama_cpp_hip, spec_litert_lm GPU SHAs, the MANUAL rows for TORCH_ROCM_WINDOWS_*/MIGRAPHX_WINDOWS_*/ORT_AMDGPU_EP_*); each spec is a separate function the tier table names, so there is nothing to fold. PRIOR: 1075 -> 1116 on 2026-09-18: +41 lines for the F1 split -- main() went 160 -> 32 lines into _parse_args, _lookup, _sweep (shared by the SAFE and REPORT tiers), _safe_row, _report_row, _print_manual, _print_unclassified, _write_phase and _lookup_verdict, with test-bump-versions.sh (40 assertions, fake specs) as the coverage the row was blocked on. The function-size.allow row and the code-complexity.allow row (cc 37) are DELETED, not re-baselined: same ONE subject, the versions.env updater. PRIOR: 1071 -> 1073 on 2026-09-18: +2 for the SCCACHE_WINDOWS_ZIP_SHA256 MANUAL registration (the retired SCCACHE_GIT_REV row was replaced). PRIOR: 1070 -> 1071 on 2026-09-17: +1 line, the two CON5 Android SDK keys (ANDROID_EXTRA_COMPILE_SDK/ANDROID_EXTRA_BUILD_TOOLS) joined the MANUAL registry so they are classified rather than reported UNCLASSIFIED. 1070 on 2026-09-11: 1136 -> 1070, the Renovate complement shrink removed the detection half (23 keys and their upstream-querying helpers); still ONE subject, the versions.env updater, so the F2 not-a-split verdict stands. 1121 -> 1136 on 2026-09-10: +15 lines, all comment, and they bought the correction of a FALSE one. The REPORT tier's shared note claimed RUFF_VERSION was report-only because 'lint-python.sh still hardcodes RUFF_PIN'. Measured: it does not and has not since 2026-08-26 -- line 61 is : "${RUFF_VERSION:?...}" and line 62 RUFF_PIN="${RUFF_VERSION}", a derivation with no literal. A tier justified by a fact that had stopped holding is the same rot the ratchets exist to catch. The note is now split per key, because the two are report-only for DIFFERENT reasons. baseline 2026-09-03: newly in scope (the scan gained *.py and Dockerfile*); F2 reviewed 2026-09-04, NOT a split target: one subject, the versions.env updater. ~370 of the 1121 lines are the spec_* table — one 5-15 line function per tracked upstream, every one of them calling the http_*/gh_*/asset_sha256 helpers defined above it. Moving the table to a sibling buys a two-way import and no comprehension: the length here is the NUMBER OF UPSTREAMS, not tangled logic. Outside the build closure, so it can be cut any day the count doubles
