s VK_KHR_surface or the xcb/xlib/wayland surfaces (arm64 and riscv64 shipped without all three). 2605 -> 2612 on 2026-09-23: the compiler battery's sanitizer case -- -fsanitize=address,undefined over the header abseil includes, libasan+libubsan NEEDED, and the binary RUN only where host == target (SAN_RUN), because qemu-user cannot host ASan/LSan. 2595 -> 2605 on 2026-09-23: _pkg_count, the one flavour-aware name match ARCH-PARITY and VENV-SET share -- the torch-stage ORT census now purges the app lock's PyPI onnxruntime-genai, which on nvidia was the only dist spelled that way (the chain's is onnxruntime-genai-cuda / -trt-rtx), so both gates count any GenAI flavour as the GenAI and every other name stays exact. 2570 -> 2595 on 2026-09-23: G1's check_ort_census (SHIPPED-TRUTH E, the ORT census run in-image; its facts and verdicts live in check-ort-provenance.sh, which this file sources) and its main() call. 2502 -> 2570 on 2026-09-23: G3's ort-crate-env consumer-contract row -- the probe fragment _consumer_ort_env_probe (split out so _consumer_contract_probe stays under 80 lines), the _consumer_ort_env_problem/_verdict pair and the row's symptom: ort-sys must link the chain ORT dynamically with pyke's download disarmed, and load-dynamic must open the chain file. PRIOR: 2454 -> 2498 on 2026-09-21/22 with the arm64 GPU runtime lane (fbc91813: the torch.version.cuda / CUDAExecutionProvider gates and the GPU-aware parity), recorded here late; 2498 -> 2502 on 2026-09-22: the ARCH-PARITY probe reports ENABLE_AMD and _parity_ort_flavor gets its rocm arm (onnxruntime_migraphx), without which the rocm wrapper could never pass its smoke. 2449 -> 2454 on 2026-09-20: the ADV/HAVE probes for PYTORCH_VERSION and TORCHVISION_VERSION, which moved the torch pair into the advertised-vs-actual gate when Dockerfile.torch started advertising them. PRIOR: 2433 -> 2449 on 2026-09-10: the consumer contract now READS the payload-off marker instead of judging an image for an SDK its build host could not install: one FACT line in the probe, a marker-first arm in _consumer_android_verdict, and the SKIP arm the loud unknown-verb default demands. 2387 -> 2433 on 2026-09-07: R1.1, the runtime-side ldd walk over /usr/local/llvm-target/bin -- the sdk stage checks NEEDED against the BUILDER's ldconfig cache, which is how liblldb shipped 3 unstartable binaries of amd64's 142. 2336 -> 2387 on 2026-09-07: VK3's toolset ratchet -- the twenty required tool names, the per-arch frozen floors (_VK_TOOLSET_FROZEN) and _vk_floor_verdict, which is the assertion that 2-of-52 could never have survived. F2 reviewed 2026-09-04 — the backlog names this as the one to split if any gets split; the review says NO. 91 functions -- 45 check_*/_probe_* assertions plus the probe-and-verdict layer they share -- over ONE image through ONE _rt_run, driven by one main(). (This row said "63 functions, all of them check_*/_probe_*" until 2026-09-07; it was never true.) Its length is the NUMBER OF ASSERTIONS about the shipped bytes, and that number growing is the gate succeeding, not debt. The only real seam is the shipped-truth payload probe -- _shipped_truth_probe / run_shipped_truth_probe and the verdict functions reading their output, named rather than line-ranged because the old ~923-1386 was ~600 lines stale by 2026-09-07 -- which collects once and derives verdicts, because a per-check exec costs a container start — that is one subject with two probe strategies, not two subjects. Splitting it would mean the file a reader opens to answer "what do we actually assert about the shipped image?" is no longer one file. HISTORY: grew 2026-09-04: HT1 check_manifest_tree_arch — the manifest-driven ELF-machine audit that generalises check_flutter/check_rust_toolchain (docs/artifact-copy-completeness.md#the-shipped-trees-must-carry-the-images-own-arch); 2026-09-04: the HT1 tree-arch scanner reads candidates (executable/.so) before the rest and a capped walk is now a FAIL, not an INFO line; 2026-09-04: check_consumer_contract — the seven-row contract a consuming CI lane depends on and cannot repair from inside a read-only overlay layer, one probe plus five pure verdict functions (docs/consumer-image-contract.md#the-contract); 2026-09-04: the consumer-contract gate gained its JDK row (probe facts, verdict, symptom); +24 for the appimagetool contract row (probe fact, verdict, symptom); +47 on 2026-09-05: the cross-payload rule the tree-arch scanner needed, and the frozen-finding table (HT2); +2 on 2026-09-05 (lane llvm-host-libs) for emptying _RT_TREE_ARCH_FROZEN and pointing it at the doc -- the five llvm-target x86-64 libs it froze are fixed at the source now (HT3); +16 on 2026-09-05 (lane ht5-vulkan) for check_vulkan_loader reading which libvulkan actually answered and the whole-tree Vulkan probe (docs/artifact-copy-completeness.md#the-vulkan-tree-ships-only-what-the-image-runs); +47 on 2026-09-05 for check_vulkan_toolset -- the loader check proved libvulkan answers, nothing asserted the prefix carries tools you can build a shader with, and a library-only prefix shipped for months (docs/vulkan-foreign-arch-sdk.md); +104 on 2026-09-05 for check_android_abi -- /opt/android is tree-arch EXEMPT because an Android payload is never the image's own arch, so nothing could see that the ABI derived from the BUILD HOST and shipped x86_64 to every image; it reads .a members too, because the object that broke a consumer's link sat inside an archive (docs/linux-cross-builds.md#the-android-abi-is-a-target-not-the-build-host); +4 on 2026-09-05 to advertise and check WASM_PACK_VERSION and FLUTTER_RUST_BRIDGE_VERSION -- the ADV/HAVE row is also the proof that the two web-lane binaries are installed at their pins; +34 on 2026-09-05 for three contract rows that ask whether a thing is STAGED rather than writable (flatpak runtimes, the AppImage runtime, the two web-lane binaries) -- one shared verdict, and their cost stays written down once in _consumer_contract_symptom
linux/scripts/tests/test-runtime-image-gates.sh | 1314 | 1301 -> 1314 on 2026-10-07: the free-threaded-python cases for the source build (python-build-standalone prefix, missing stdlib module, no build fact). PRIOR: 1285 -> 1301 on 2026-10-06: CON66's free-threaded-python cases. PRIOR: 1259 -> 1285 on 2026-10-06: CON65's cargo-qa-tools cases beside the chrome and emulator ones. PRIOR: 1254 -> 1259 on 2026-10-05: CON61 -- one t_needs line under each of the five cases whose scanner output a Windows python3 prints with drive-letter paths. PRIOR: 1217 -> 1254 on 2026-10-01: CON48 boot cases, the vkarch probe run end to end through _gate, stacked on CON50 -- the chrome and android-emulator rows' cases (pass on amd64/arm64, each BAD edit, the riscv64 and arm64 exemptions and their rot, the facts from a real probe run), plus _t_edit_table and _CC_PROBE_FNS, which the G3 table and every probe run now share. PRIOR: 1209 -> 1114 on 2026-09-30: comment sweep. PRIOR: 1210 -> 1209 on 2026-09-30: the four shipped-loader cases share _vk_shipped (code-dupes). 1169 -> 1210 on 2026-09-30: CON41 -- the WSI verdict's cases (the measured WSI-less arm64 list fails, one missing surface fails, a prefix-only match does not count, no list at all fails) and a VKEXT line in the existing loader fixtures. 1161 -> 1169 on 2026-09-23: the ort-crate-env row now tells an unset ORT_LIB_PATH/CARGO_NET_OFFLINE from a set-but-EMPTY one (ort-sys reads the empty value: an empty ORT_LIB_PATH outranks ORT_LIB_LOCATION, an empty CARGO_NET_OFFLINE re-arms the download), so the fixture carries both '<unset>' lines, the host probe run asserts the marker and the empty value, and the BAD table gained the empty, missing-line and yes/on cases. 1107 -> 1161 on 2026-09-23: the G3 ort-crate-env cases -- a healthy row, nine BAD edits (unset/foreign lib dir, no link library, a non-chain dylib, static link, armed download, ORT_LIB_PATH, a false CARGO_NET_OFFLINE), the NOFACT case, and the ORT facts asserted on the existing host probe run; every probe site now extracts _consumer_ort_env_probe too. PRIOR: 1086 -> 1107 on 2026-09-10: the _cc_android fixtures gained the payload-off knob plus the two cases that make the new fact non-vacuous: a recorded yes SKIPs, and a MISSING fact is NOFACT rather than a silent grant. 1048 -> 1086 on 2026-09-07: the llvm-target startability cases -- clean, the liblldb shape, a probe that did not run, an absent prefix, and the call site in main(). 1005 -> 1048 on 2026-09-07: the five frozen-floor cases -- a prefix that keeps every required NAME can still lose tools, which is what 2-of-52 looked like, so the floors get their own below/at/above cases plus the amd64 row and the no-row arch; 985 -> 1005 on 2026-09-07: the verdict-vocabulary case -- baseline 2026-09-05: the suite that proves smoke-runtime-image.sh's gates can fail, and its length is the same number its subject's row is — one _extract of the real function plus stubs per assertion, 76 t_cases over seven gate families (WE/WF healthcheck and wheel ratchet, XQ default boot, advertised keys, HT1 tree-arch and its host-side halves, the consumer contract). Splitting by family is possible but buys nothing: the _extract harness and its stub table are shared by all of them, so seven files would each re-source it and the reader loses the one place that answers "what makes these gates bite?". 767 -> 837 on 2026-09-05 for the cross-payload arm of the tree-arch gate; 837 -> 872 on 2026-09-05 (lane ht5-vulkan) for the four Vulkan-loader verdicts and the un-narrowed tree probe; 872 -> 917 on 2026-09-05 for the seven check_vulkan_toolset cases -- the gate that fails on the shape that actually shipped (a target SDK prefix with full libraries and two binaries), with its required/reported lists read out of the source so the suite cannot drift from it (docs/vulkan-foreign-arch-sdk.md); 917 -> 966 on 2026-09-05 for the seven check_android_abi cases, including the mixed-payload one -- one stale ABI among many is how the wrong objects actually reached a consumer, and the shipped/fixed fixtures are hoisted so the two verdicts about the same payload are not two copies of it; +18 on 2026-09-06 for the exemption-handoff case -- /opt/android leaves tree-arch and check_android_abi takes it over, which is only honest while that gate actually walks the tree
linux/scripts/02-toolchain/vulkan.sh | 888 | 1065 -> 888 on 2026-09-30: comment sweep. PRIOR: 1039 -> 1065 on 2026-09-30: CON41 -- the target loader is built with X11/XCB/Wayland WSI, and _vulkan_loader_wsi_missing reads the installed libvulkan.so.1's exports so a loader that dropped a surface type fails the REQUIRED verdict instead of shipping. 1010 -> 1039 on 2026-09-10 (rebase): both same-day bumps in one file -- VK6/VK7 below AND the WSI dev packages for a target that IS the build host. Neither side's count survived the merge (1008 and 1010); 1039 is measured. Their half: install the WSI dev packages for the host-target case too (the old cross_build_is_active guard skipped them by definition when target==build host), plus a three-line presence report for the link-time symlinks so a repeat of "cannot find -lxcb" is diagnosable from the log instead of costing another 7 h run. 964 -> 979 on 2026-09-09: LIBRARY_PATH plus an explicit -L for the native-target case. Once the wrong-arch libxcb was correctly ignored the link found NOTHING: pkg-config returns a bare XCB_LIBRARIES=xcb with the directory in a separate XCB_LIBRARY_DIRS, and the failing line carried no -L at all. Both mechanisms because LIBRARY_PATH is honoured by the compiler DRIVER only. 946 -> 964 on 2026-09-09 (rebase): both same-day bumps landed in one file -- VK4 below AND the native-ARM-host CMAKE_IGNORE_PATH from the other branch. Neither side's count survived the merge (930 and 946); 964 is measured, not added up. 944 -> 946 on 2026-09-09: CMAKE_REQUIRE_FIND_PACKAGE_Qt6 for vulkantools plus the comment saying why it is load-bearing -- upstream find_package(Qt6 QUIET) drops the whole configurator with a message() and exits 0, so the row would count as BUILT while the SDK ships no vkconfig. 912 -> 930 (their branch, same day): 912 -> 930 on 2026-09-09: CMAKE_IGNORE_PATH for the foreign multiarch lib dirs when the cross TARGET is the build host itself. A native arm64 build makes amd64 a real cross target, so its dev packages are installed system-wide; CMAKE_LIBRARY_ARCHITECTURE is only a preference, so find_library still reached /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu and handed vulkaninfo an x86_64 libxcb.so, failing the link with "file in wrong format" after vulkan-tools had otherwise built. Gated on target==build host, so it is inert on the amd64 dev box, where for_each_cross_target skips the host arch entirely. 904 -> 912 on 2026-09-08: the WGPU exception for arches with no Dawn prebuilt. slang-rhi composes a download URL for a PREBUILT Dawn WebGPU zip and upstream ships x86_64/aarch64 only; its arch cascade FATAL_ERRORs on anything else UNCONDITIONALLY, so the backend option alone is not enough and SLANG_RHI_DAWN_URL has to be defined too or the cascade is still entered. That FATAL_ERROR is what kept slang off riscv64 after the slang.h patch already worked. Arch-conditional on purpose, and a test asserts aarch64 KEEPS its WebGPU. 899 -> 904 on 2026-09-08: _vulkan_patch_component, the upstream-defect hook. slang's pinned source (SDK 1.4.357.0 pins commit 84792eb15, three weeks before the fix merged) derives pointer size and byte order from a whitelist with no __riscv arm, so riscv64 hits `#error "Couldn't determine endianness"` AND a silent 32-bit SlangInt -- proved by running the pinned macro block through cpp. Backport of upstream PR #12305; the table saying when each patch becomes droppable is docs/vulkan-foreign-arch-sdk.md#upstream-patches-recheck-on-every-sdk-bump. Net +5 after the arch-skip comment shrank into that doc. 883 -> 899 on 2026-09-08: the four defects the first VK2 chain measured BEHIND the routes, +16 lines. Each route worked and each component then died at something new: jsoncpp's archive was not PIC so it could not enter libVkLayer_khronos_profiles.so (fix is one shared -DCMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE=ON, not a per-row flag, because any archive we hand the SDK can land in a layer .so); gfxreconstruct found every target LIB but no GL HEADERS, so the include bridge grew GL/KHR/EGL/GLES2/GLES3; vulkancapsviewer's upstream interpolates ${VULKAN_LOADER_INSTALL_DIR}/lib/libvulkan.so RAW and unset resolves to the host path; slang needed ./vulkansdk's own between-build-and-install copy step, which is the _xbuild_extra_targets array and its loop. 809 -> 883 on 2026-09-07: VK2's four remaining components -- the two config-package rows, _vulkan_target_dynamic_args (the Canadian-cross paths a static table cannot carry) and the required-component verdict with its _vk_note_failure owner 912 -> 944 on 2026-09-09: VK4 -- the three components LunarG's own build_all builds and this list never checked out. The 15-binary gap between x86_64/bin (52) and the foreign arches (37) is exactly dxc (12 dx* aliases + llvm-tblgen) and vulkantools (vkconfig, vkconfig-gui); the 4 missing layers are 3 more from vulkantools plus crash-diagnostic-layer, and yaml-cpp is CDL's dependency. Four table rows plus three dynamic-arg arms, because all three need PATHS a static table cannot carry: Qt6 host tooling and the raw loader path for vulkantools (the same pair vcv needed), the install dirs for CDL, and for dxc both the vendor -C cache file (most of its options do not exist until it is read) and the two host tblgens (an LLVM 3.7 fork -- the same Canadian cross llvm-cross.sh and slang already do). The table is now 21 rows + 3 hardwired = 24, which is exactly the count of BUILD_* flags in the vendor script's build_all. 904 -> 912 on 2026-09-08: the WGPU exception for arches with no Dawn prebuilt. slang-rhi composes a download URL for a PREBUILT Dawn WebGPU zip and upstream ships x86_64/aarch64 only; its arch cascade FATAL_ERRORs on anything else UNCONDITIONALLY, so the backend option alone is not enough and SLANG_RHI_DAWN_URL has to be defined too or the cascade is still entered. That FATAL_ERROR is what kept slang off riscv64 after the slang.h patch already worked. Arch-conditional on purpose, and a test asserts aarch64 KEEPS its WebGPU. 899 -> 904 on 2026-09-08: _vulkan_patch_component, the upstream-defect hook. slang's pinned source (SDK 1.4.357.0 pins commit 84792eb15, three weeks before the fix merged) derives pointer size and byte order from a whitelist with no __riscv arm, so riscv64 hits `#error "Couldn't determine endianness"` AND a silent 32-bit SlangInt -- proved by running the pinned macro block through cpp. Backport of upstream PR #12305; the table saying when each patch becomes droppable is docs/vulkan-foreign-arch-sdk.md#upstream-patches-recheck-on-every-sdk-bump. Net +5 after the arch-skip comment shrank into that doc. 883 -> 899 on 2026-09-08: the four defects the first VK2 chain measured BEHIND the routes, +16 lines. Each route worked and each component then died at something new: jsoncpp's archive was not PIC so it could not enter libVkLayer_khronos_profiles.so (fix is one shared -DCMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE=ON, not a per-row flag, because any archive we hand the SDK can land in a layer .so); gfxreconstruct found every target LIB but no GL HEADERS, so the include bridge grew GL/KHR/EGL/GLES2/GLES3; vulkancapsviewer's upstream interpolates ${VULKAN_LOADER_INSTALL_DIR}/lib/libvulkan.so RAW and unset resolves to the host path; slang needed ./vulkansdk's own between-build-and-install copy step, which is the _xbuild_extra_targets array and its loop. 809 -> 883 on 2026-09-07: VK2's four remaining components -- the two config-package rows, _vulkan_target_dynamic_args (the Canadian-cross paths a static table cannot carry) and the required-component verdict with its _vk_note_failure owner. baseline 2026-09-05: one subject -- provision the Vulkan SDK for the host AND cross-build the target-arch prefix the image runs. The two halves share the SDK layout, the checkout names and the pkg-config environment that has to differ between them, which is exactly the bug that cost the sdk stage a run; splitting them would put that shared contract in two files. Grew past 800 when the target build stopped being four components and became the whole SDK (docs/vulkan-foreign-arch-sdk.md). 996 -> 1010 on 2026-09-09: VK6 -- glslang is configured TWICE into one prefix (shared then static; BUILD_SHARED_LIBS is exclusive, so ON alone would trade six static installs for nine shared ones, and the static pass must land LAST because it owns the exported CMake package). Plus SPIRV_CROSS_SHARED=ON, which is purely additive. 979 -> 996 on 2026-09-09: VK7 -- _vulkan_target_prune_nonsdk_dxc plus its call, the mirror of the BUILD_DXC arm of LunarG's own clean_nonsdk_files (vendor vulkansdk:519-528). The dxc row installs the LLVM 3.7 fork's include/{clang,clang-c,llvm,llvm-c} and four validator libs into the TARGET prefix; ./vulkansdk deletes exactly those eight from the prefix it builds, so the amd64 tarball has never carried them and only the foreign arches did. It belongs in this file because the eight paths are pinned to today's vendor script and have to be re-read on the next VULKAN_VERSION bump, next to the rest of the SDK contract. 964 -> 979 on 2026-09-09: LIBRARY_PATH plus an explicit -L for the native-target case. Once the wrong-arch libxcb was correctly ignored the link found NOTHING: pkg-config returns a bare XCB_LIBRARIES=xcb with the directory in a separate XCB_LIBRARY_DIRS, and the failing line carried no -L at all. Both mechanisms because LIBRARY_PATH is honoured by the compiler DRIVER only. 946 -> 964 on 2026-09-09 (rebase): both same-day bumps landed in one file -- VK4 below AND the native-ARM-host CMAKE_IGNORE_PATH from the other branch. Neither side's count survived the merge (930 and 946); 964 is measured, not added up. 944 -> 946 on 2026-09-09: CMAKE_REQUIRE_FIND_PACKAGE_Qt6 for vulkantools plus the comment saying why it is load-bearing -- upstream find_package(Qt6 QUIET) drops the whole configurator with a message() and exits 0, so the row would count as BUILT while the SDK ships no vkconfig. 912 -> 930 (their branch, same day): 912 -> 930 on 2026-09-09: CMAKE_IGNORE_PATH for the foreign multiarch lib dirs when the cross TARGET is the build host itself. A native arm64 build makes amd64 a real cross target, so its dev packages are installed system-wide; CMAKE_LIBRARY_ARCHITECTURE is only a preference, so find_library still reached /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu and handed vulkaninfo an x86_64 libxcb.so, failing the link with "file in wrong format" after vulkan-tools had otherwise built. Gated on target==build host, so it is inert on the amd64 dev box, where for_each_cross_target skips the host arch entirely. 904 -> 912 on 2026-09-08: the WGPU exception for arches with no Dawn prebuilt. slang-rhi composes a download URL for a PREBUILT Dawn WebGPU zip and upstream ships x86_64/aarch64 only; its arch cascade FATAL_ERRORs on anything else UNCONDITIONALLY, so the backend option alone is not enough and SLANG_RHI_DAWN_URL has to be defined too or the cascade is still entered. That FATAL_ERROR is what kept slang off riscv64 after the slang.h patch already worked. Arch-conditional on purpose, and a test asserts aarch64 KEEPS its WebGPU. 899 -> 904 on 2026-09-08: _vulkan_patch_component, the upstream-defect hook. slang's pinned source (SDK 1.4.357.0 pins commit 84792eb15, three weeks before the fix merged) derives pointer size and byte order from a whitelist with no __riscv arm, so riscv64 hits `#error "Couldn't determine endianness"` AND a silent 32-bit SlangInt -- proved by running the pinned macro block through cpp. Backport of upstream PR #12305; the table saying when each patch becomes droppable is docs/vulkan-foreign-arch-sdk.md#upstream-patches-recheck-on-every-sdk-bump. Net +5 after the arch-skip comment shrank into that doc. 883 -> 899 on 2026-09-08: the four defects the first VK2 chain measured BEHIND the routes, +16 lines. Each route worked and each component then died at something new: jsoncpp's archive was not PIC so it could not enter libVkLayer_khronos_profiles.so (fix is one shared -DCMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE=ON, not a per-